## Linker version script for the shared C module.
##
## Without it the library exported all 834 symbols it contains, and only 11 of
## those are ours - the rest is the whole Wasmtime C API. ELF resolves a
## library's own calls through the global scope, so a program that defined any
## of those names, or linked its own Wasmtime, took over the calls libzuid makes
## internally. With a different Wasmtime version that means mismatched ABIs
## rather than a clean failure.
##
## 'local: *' is the half that matters most: everything not named below becomes
## local, so libzuid's internal calls bind inside the library and cannot be
## interposed at all.

{
	global:
		zuid_*;
	local:
		*;
};
